        "source_span": "Plant cells and animal cells are similar in many ways \u2014 both contain a nucleus, cytoplasm, mitochondria, and a cell membrane. But there is one important difference: plant cells have an extra layer outside the cell membrane called the cell wall. The cell wall is rigid and gives the plant cell a fixed shape and extra protection, which is one reason plants can grow tall and stand upright."
